172	african_arguments	166	https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/tigrays-lost-classrooms-why-education-must-be-at-the-centre-of-recovery/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tigrays-lost-classrooms-why-education-must-be-a	Tigray’s Lost Classrooms: Why Education Must Be at the Centre of Recovery <p>The war in Tigray did not only destroy lives, homes, hospitals and livelihoods. It also attacked the foundations of the region’s future by depriving an entire generation of children of education. In January 2025, the European Commission’s Directorate-General for European Civil Protection and Humanitarian Aid Operations reported that approximately 2.4 million school-aged children in Tigray had been denied education for three academic years. It also reported that 88 per cent of the region’s school infrastructure had been damaged. These figures describe more than an interruption to schooling. They reveal a generational emergency whose consequences may shape Tigray for decades. The [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/tigrays-lost-classrooms-why-education-must-be-at-the-centre-of-recovery/">Tigray’s Lost Classrooms: Why Education Must Be at the Centre of Recovery</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	en	\N	\N	https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/tigrays-lost-classrooms-why-education-must-be-at-the-centre-of-recovery/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tigrays-lost-classrooms-why-education-must-be-at-the-centre-of-recovery	2026-07-25 13:20:14+00	2026-08-02 09:30:12.097403+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK	neutral	0.015	[{"text": "Tigray", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Lost Classrooms", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Why Education Must Be", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Centre", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Recovery", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "The", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "In January", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "European Commission", "label": "PERSON"}