175	african_arguments	169	https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/the-ocean-is-not-fragmented-power-is/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=the-ocean-is-not-fragmented-power-is	The Ocean Is Not Fragmented. Power Is. <p>On 16-18 June in Mombasa, the Our Ocean Conference met on African soil for the first time, and over 100 governments, businesses and civil society organisations announced 320 new commitments valued at $6.4 billion to advance ocean conservation, sustainable fisheries, climate resilience and the blue economy. I have sat in enough such rooms to know the applause is not the test. Driving back along the coast afterwards, I kept turning over a thought that fits no panel agenda: the ocean is not fragmented: our power over it is. The sea moves as one system. Our institutions arrive carved into ministries, budgets, [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/the-ocean-is-not-fragmented-power-is/">The Ocean Is Not Fragmented. Power Is.</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	en	\N	\N	https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/the-ocean-is-not-fragmented-power-is/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=the-ocean-is-not-fragmented-power-is	2026-07-15 10:20:57+00	2026-08-02 09:30:12.172754+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK	neutral	0.0795	[{"text": "The Ocean Is Not Fragmented", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Power Is", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Mombasa", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Our Ocean Conference", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Driving", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "The", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Our", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "African Arguments", "label": "PERSON"}]	["ocean", "fragmented", "power", "african", "mombasa", "conference", "soil", "governments", "businesses", "civil"]	["economic_development"]	t	2026-08-02 09:31:18.979448+00
