177	african_arguments	170	https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/sixty-six-years-on-the-promise-of-somali-independence-remains-unfulfilled/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sixty-six-years-on-the-promise-of-somali-inde	Sixty-Six Years On, the Promise of Somali Independence Remains Unfulfilled. <p>A Night of Hope. Aweys Addow, who was 19 years old when the flag was hoisted, was present to witness the event at Ficho Goberno, the former site of Mogadishu&#8217;s mayoral residence. At 12:00 hours (midnight) on 1 July 1960, Addow was among hundreds of jubilant Somalis who came out to celebrate the birth of the new nation, believing, with the rest of his generation, that Somalia had finally entered a new era based on unity, freedom and national pride. A unified, ethnically homogeneous Somalia composed of all the Somali people and the unification of the other Somali-inhabited areas of [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/sixty-six-years-on-the-promise-of-somali-independence-remains-unfulfilled/">Sixty-Six Years On, the Promise of Somali Independence Remains Unfulfilled.</a> appeared first on <a href="https://africanarguments.org">African Arguments</a>.</p>	en	\N	\N	https://africanarguments.org/2026/07/sixty-six-years-on-the-promise-of-somali-independence-remains-unfulfilled/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sixty-six-years-on-the-promise-of-somali-independence-remains-unfulfilled	2026-07-14 12:05:41+00	2026-08-02 09:30:12.220196+00	african_arguments:Nigeria diaspora community UK	neutral	0.0622	[{"text": "Sixty", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Six Years On", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Promise", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Somali Independence Remains Unfulfilled", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Night", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Hope", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Aweys Addow", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Ficho Goberno", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Mogadishu", "label": "PERSON"}, {"text": "Addow", "label": "PER